<!-- WipEout Omega Collection (CUSA07671 01.07): render resolution patches, found on the US eboot.bin with sha256
     3a52e910f6c450cc2f0c85ef994be5d8c951c326a362bcc4775f29e6ff7f644c. Each site is found by its signature
     (Pattern/At); Address is that build's address.

     How the game sizes its picture:
     - The output size is chosen at 0x7fa2e4 from the video-out resolution status:
         w = max(status.w, 1920); h = max(status.h, 1080); base PS4: w = min(w, 1920), h = min(h, 1080)
       and stored to two 16-bit globals that the buffer setup at 0x7fbdd0 reads. The patch raises the
       minimum, the cap and the compare of both.
     - Half-resolution buffers are hardcoded 960x540 (0x6446xx, 0x64b5xx). They must stay half of the output:
       0x7e29c0 picks one of four variants by (2*half < full) per axis from a table whose mismatch entries are
       null, so without them the game crashes at start (null read at 0x7e2a0a).
     - The cameras pick their aspect ratio from 16/9 (one player), 32/9 or 8/9 (split screen halves) next to
       pi/360, at 0x3adb86 and 0x3af3e7. Both 16/9 floats must change together: changing one alone smears
       the picture horizontally (presumably the motion blur reprojection). The vertical field of view is
       fixed, so a wider aspect ratio widens the view (Hor+) with no camera code changes. The split screen
       ratios are untouched.

     - From 3840 pixels wide the game sets a "4K mode" flag (0x1212c39, at 0x7fb657: (field & 0xff00) > 0xeff),
       read at about 55 sites. With it the scene renders at half width with checkerboard and a compute resolve
       (the Pro path); without it, at full resolution with 4-sample depth as in the 1080p mode. The separate
       "Native 4K rendering (no checkerboard)" patch keeps the flag false; with checkerboard, one R32Uint resolve
       buffer stays 1920x2160 (half of 3840), which this file does not size.

     Not handled: the 2D layer (HUD, menus) is a 1920x1080 canvas set up at three inlined sites
     ([obj+0x2c]=1920.0f, [obj+0x30]=1080.0f, int16 rect at +0x34: 0x4f17c0, 0x5c6fad, 0x7515b4); its elements
     sit at absolute 1920-space positions, so widening the canvas alone moves right-anchored elements.

     Tested in game on Windows (RTX 4090) in single races (HD/2048 Metro Park, Campaign): 2560x1080 and
     5120x2160. Not tested: CUSA05670 (EU), split screen, replays, every event type. -->
<Patch>
    <TitleID>
        <ID>CUSA07671</ID>
        <ID>CUSA05670</ID>
    </TitleID>
    <Metadata Title="WipEout Omega Collection" Name="Resolution Patch - 2560x1080" Note="Renders at 2560x1080 (2.370:1): output and half-resolution buffers at that size and the camera aspect ratio set to match. The camera keeps its vertical field of view, so the wider picture shows more at the sides (Hor+). HUD and menus are still laid out for 16:9 and appear stretched." Author="d4g" PatchVer="1.0" AppVer="01.00" AppElf="eboot.bin" isEnabled="false">
